"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:G1G2","usage":{"input_tokens":411439,"output_tokens":4380,"requests":9}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"62a4edfc6225c30c924c85bce682e3706e573e15fb5c1d7fbf7e799ba333f925"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T5c","usage":{"input_tokens":28939,"output_tokens":1092,"requests":3}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"bba1654a873e5a540da4824392dd265f4d66ffab042e25d720c50134074760a3"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:G6","usage":{"input_tokens":226571,"output_tokens":5384,"requests":7}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"f324cdec9b49b176f399d01e9b8c6c5840c0d03eef2cbe0fe7ab6908f64084ce"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:project.symbol-reference-completeness","usage":{"input_tokens":193771,"output_tokens":1932,"requests":5}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"State where the mcp-scoped backoff GATE lives (a read-and-skip check inside the mcp block, keyed to the new mcp backoff file) so an open mcp window skips only the mcp deploy without stopping the tick, mirroring the bot gate moved into the bot block.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.0,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'This change re-points the mcp block's sites to a new mcp-scoped recorder ... which is what makes it safe to move its gate from the top of the script into the bot block.' — describes the recorder + the BOT gate move, not an mcp gate.","Code: the only backoff gate is the top-of-script `if [ \"$bo_sha\" = \"$TARGET\" ] && ... exit 0` at :484-486, reading the shared BACKOFF_FILE.","Additional AC `test_mcp_backoff_window_skips_the_mcp_deploy_without_stopping_the_tick` and `test_an_open_bot_backoff_with_no_pending_delta_is_not_reported_as_a_skip` presuppose a per-component gate the fix narrative does not place."],"finding":"The 'Failure' rework specifies a new mcp-scoped backoff RECORDER and relocates the shared backoff GATE (:484-486) into the bot block, but never says where the mcp backoff GATE (the read-and-skip check consuming the new mcp file) is placed. Without an mcp-scoped gate inside the mcp block, the mcp recorder writes state nothing reads, so an mcp backoff window would not actually skip the mcp deploy.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa832a214b85954c4","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Proposed fix / 'Scope growth' → Failure; mcp block infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh:625-717 (failure sites :631-:703, current gate :484-486)","norm_id":"n0241b7fc59a38c65","priority":0.8,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An mcp deploy fails, writing the mcp-scoped backoff; on the next tick with the same TARGET the mcp block should skip within its window but, with no mcp gate, re-attempts every tick.","A bot-only change on a tick where mcp is inside its backoff window — expected mcp skip vs. actual behaviour is unspecified."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"In the mcp block, before starting the blue-green cutover, add an mcp-scoped gate that reads the new mcp backoff file and, when its window is open for TARGET, skips the mcp deploy (not the whole tick) — symmetric to the relocated bot gate; and confirm the mcp failure sites keep `exit 1` for fail-closed-per-component behaviour while writing the mcp-scoped file.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"Add an acceptance criterion (with a named proof test) that a component which successfully deployed on one tick computes no delta and is SKIPPED on the next, and one covering the absent-marker fallback to $DEPLOYED on the first post-upgrade tick.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["E1","E6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'each component's delta gate is RE-POINTED to diff from that marker ... so a component already at $TARGET computes no delta and is skipped'","The additional ACs enumerate deferral, mcp-failure-no-backoff, failed-mcp-no-bot-redeploy, backoff-skip cases — none asserts a SUCCESSFULLY deployed component computes no delta and is skipped on the subsequent tick","'An absent or unparseable marker falls back to $DEPLOYED' has no covering criterion for the first-tick-after-upgrade behavior"],"finding":"The 'Completion' fix re-points each component's delta gate to diff from its own marker so 'a component already at $TARGET computes no delta and is skipped', but no acceptance criterion verifies the core success case: a component that deployed on one tick is NOT redeployed on the next. The additional ACs cover deferral (markers unadvanced), failures, and backoff-skips, but not the ordinary complete-then-skip path the marker mechanism exists to produce.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f27b04ecaa59b6023","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope growth across review rounds -> Completion; Additional acceptance criteria","norm_id":"n7f6e51a6ce86660d","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Tick N deploys the bot; tick N+1 must skip it (no stop-and-drain that kills an in-flight review, bug 34cd)","First tick after upgrade with no marker present must decide identically to today"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add: '[ ] A component that deployed on tick N is skipped on tick N+1 (no redeploy). Proof: test_completed_component_is_not_redeployed_next_tick' and '[ ] With no marker present, both gates fall back to $DEPLOYED and decide as today. Proof: test_absent_marker_falls_back_to_deployed_baseline'.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"Add regression coverage for the absent/unparseable per-component marker case, asserting the delta gate falls back to $DEPLOYED and decides identically to the pre-fix behaviour.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T12","T6","T9","necessity","project.portability"],"criteria":["E5"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.075,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'An absent or unparseable marker falls back to $DEPLOYED, so the first tick after upgrade decides exactly as it does today.'","No acceptance criterion or named test exercises the absent/unparseable-marker fallback path."],"finding":"The plan states 'An absent or unparseable marker falls back to $DEPLOYED, so the first tick after upgrade decides exactly as it does today' — a new fallback branch introduced by re-pointing the delta gate to per-component markers. This branch (missing/unparseable marker → fall back to global $DEPLOYED) has no named test in the acceptance criteria; the listed tests all assume markers exist. The first-tick-after-upgrade case is exactly where the marker files do not yet exist.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4932be22334afe43","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"'Completion' paragraph under Scope growth / Additional acceptance criteria","norm_id":"n7bdd12b571f9b226","priority":0.875,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add a test (e.g. test_first_tick_after_upgrade_with_no_component_marker_falls_back_to_deployed) that runs a tick with no bot-deployed-sha/mcp-deployed-sha files and asserts the delta is computed from $DEPLOYED.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["2 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"Capture the per-component deploy-state model (markers, per-component backoff, incompleteness flags, footer guard invariants) in a short comment block or design note referenced from the plan.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["T5e"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'ONE piece of global state standing in for TWO independently-deploying components'","New surfaces introduced: per-component markers, mcp-scoped record_backoff_failure, bot_incomplete/mcp_incomplete, re-pointed changed_range calls","No documentation deliverable is mentioned anywhere in the plan"],"finding":"The plan splits ONE global state variable into per-component markers, a new mcp-scoped backoff recorder, and bot_incomplete/mcp_incomplete flags — a meaningful pattern change to how autodeploy tracks per-component deploy state across ticks — but names no ADR / AGENTS.md / design-doc update capturing the new per-component state model. Four review rounds re-derived this same shape, evidence the invariant is non-obvious to future readers.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f7704cc12cc199f73","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope growth across review rounds","norm_id":"nb535d4d8176ee365","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future editor touches the footer or a gate without knowing markers must stay unadvanced on deferred/incomplete ticks and re-introduces a coupling bug"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Add a header comment in autodeploy.sh (or an AGENTS.md/ADR note) documenting: each component advances its own marker only on completion; deferred/incomplete ticks preserve markers and DEFER_FILE; delta gates diff from per-component markers with $DEPLOYED fallback.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2857,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"Broaden the title/summary to reflect that the change also splits completion markers, splits the shared backoff, and adds per-component incompleteness tracking — not only the deferral exit-0 fix.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T12","T6","T9","necessity","project.portability"],"criteria":["E3"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Title: 'a review-bot deferral exit 0s the script, so the independent mcp blue-green deploy never runs'","Body: 'This change re-points the mcp block's sites to a new mcp-scoped recorder', 'each component now records its own marker', 'bot_incomplete / mcp_incomplete mark it and the footer guard honours both'"],"finding":"The title scopes the change narrowly to the deferral exit-0 fix ('a review-bot deferral exit 0s the script, so the independent mcp blue-green deploy never runs'), but the body — under 'Scope growth across review rounds' — also re-points each component's delta gate to per-component markers, splits the shared backoff into an mcp-scoped recorder, and adds bot_incomplete/mcp_incomplete tracking. The body does materially MORE than the headline promises; the title should reflect the broadened scope so a reader knows the ticket touches completion-marker, backoff, and incompleteness semantics, not just control flow.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f07d35b263a437ec5","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Title / 'Scope growth across review rounds'","norm_id":"nff49ec0bbb1397ef","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Retitle to something like 'autodeploy: make the bot and mcp deploys independent — scope deferral, completion markers, and backoff per-component'.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.4286,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"State explicitly whether the backoff-split and incompleteness-tracking must ship atomically with the deferral fix (order-coupled) or could land as follow-on children.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T12","T6","T9","necessity","project.portability"],"criteria":["G5"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.6429,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'an mcp failure throttled the BOT and a bot failure suppressed mcp' — a backoff-scoping bug distinct from the deferral exit-0 bug","'Four review rounds each found the same shape, each fix exposing the next'","Three separate bug shapes (Completion, Failure, Incompleteness) each with their own acceptance criteria."],"finding":"Under 'Scope growth across review rounds' the plan bundles three distinct defects with distinct reasons-to-change: (1) the deferral exit-0 reachability fix, (2) mcp failures writing the SHARED backoff and throttling the bot (and vice-versa), and (3) the footer stamping a marker for a deploy that never ran (permanent-drop). The plan argues each 'exposed the next', and the completion-marker split is plausibly order-coupled to (1) (else bug 34cd), but the backoff-split (2) targets a bug that exists independently of the deferral fix. Confirm the backoff-split and incompleteness-tracking are genuinely order-coupled to the deferral fix rather than independently releasable, or split them out.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"feb95702d4f063856","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"'Scope growth across review rounds'","norm_id":"n7ccea58e0c917c9a","priority":0.1571,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2857,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"bundles_separable_slices","vague_directive":"none"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"7af436f3dce234e3","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["f39e633ee4778796",7909],"description_boxes":["05a8475feebbfea6",0],"file_impact":["963a011d30cb3d0c",2],"ticket_id":["ea5b34bdf1fb71f0",19]},"metrics":{"cache_read_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"claim_path":"no-llm/no-network (structural; the fast claim check is a local HMAC verify)","det_ms":2998.8,"input_tokens":1384666,"llm_calls":28,"llm_ms":314592.1,"output_tokens":31482,"precheck":{"cited_anchor_warning":false},"total_ms":329240.8,"verify_requests":23},"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","priority_floor":0.8,"provider_provenance":{"candidates":["bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6"],"capabilities":{"nat